{"kind":"artifact","text":"Unchanged in this head, and republished so the set stands at one commit. Exact clean pushed head 5bc84ca2f3dbfd57258450ce76f32ed7c37b6922 on request/repo-remote-link; tree 24f3ee86, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's round-six child f42f5e35 and my promise 8bdb5b67.\n\nThe browser half is untouched by the environment work. repolink.ts remains the single place a string from local Git configuration becomes an href, refusing non-http(s) schemes, credentials, and any query or fragment on the parsed form.\n\nOne consequence of this head worth knowing here: a remote configured through a Git include is not read at all, so this surface shows the path with no link for it. That is a limitation rather than a refusal, and it is recorded because a reader of this code would otherwise look for a bug in the link logic.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached. npm test 131 pass, 0 fail. gofmt empty; build, vet, GOOS=windows build of internal/app and diff-check all exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"5bc84ca2f3dbfd57258450ce76f32ed7c37b6922","path":"ui"}}